  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "SUBJECTIVE INTERVAL HISTORY",
      "text": "SUBJECTIVE INTERVAL HISTORY: Patient Sarah Martin presents for longitudinal chronic disease management. Since the last comprehensive visit three months ago, the patient reports adherence to diet and exercise recommendations. Recent outpatient send-out interval laboratory check showed potassium of 4.01 mmol/L. Concurrent testing noted that fasting calcium was 8.98 mg/dL. The patient denies any acute side effects or hypoglycemic episodes."
    },
    {
      "title": "CLINICAL COURSE & PROGRESSION",
      "text": "CLINICAL COURSE & PROGRESSION: Over the preceding quarter, therapy with Azithromycin at 250 mg orally once daily for 5 days was maintained. In-clinic point-of-care glucose was 88.2 mg/dL, confirming steady metabolic control. Vascular and sensory examinations of bilateral feet were normal without neuropathy."
    },
    {
      "title": "UPDATED CHRONIC MEDICATION PLAN",
      "text": "UPDATED CHRONIC MEDICATION PLAN: Refills were renewed for Metoprolol 100 mg orally twice daily, as well as Amlodipine 2.5 mg PO every morning. Patient demonstrated proper technique and confirmed understanding of morning versus evening administration."
    },
    {
      "title": "FOLLOW-UP & COORDINATION",
      "text": "Return to clinic in six months for repeat comprehensive metabolic panel and lipid panel. Routine health maintenance screenings were reviewed and scheduled."
    }
  ],
